    "_comment": "Countries with no Amazon storefront of their own, served by another marketplace as an export destination. The distinction matters: the landed price is not the listed price, and the listed currency is not necessarily the marketplace's home currency.",
    "IL": {
      "served_by": "amazon-us",
      "notes": [
        "There is no amazon.co.il. Israel is served by amazon.com as an international destination.",
        "amazon.com renders prices in ILS when the request egresses from an Israeli IP, and in USD from a US IP. Same URL, same ASIN, different number, HTTP 200 either way - so the currency in the answer is a property of the route, not of the listing. Verified via the geo-egress work; see reference/fetch-routes.md.",
        "Landed cost adds an Import Fees Deposit plus shipping. The listed price is not the price paid.",
        "Prime does not carry over. A US Prime membership buys nothing on an order shipped to Israel."
